  "review_summary": "The corrected rationale addresses each of the three error targets. It removes the unsupported inference that the authors 'know exactly what to do' and replaces it with an acknowledgment that the comment defers concrete details to the cited paper. It corrects the rubric misapplication by noting the action is explicit but vague on execution rather than fully concrete. It also revises the unsupported conclusion of 'fully actionable' to a more accurate statement that actionability is limited by the lack of concrete guidance. The rationale preserves the original correct identification of the explicit action (rephrasing the assumption per Lachapelle et al., 2023) and does not state a numeric score or gold label. The text is coherent and suitable for insertion as a Qwen3-4B rescoring rationale."
